From c455d58dd38852fef814abde428c8f3040cac33d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 14:59:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03480/11362] [outer-loop] #2 Go-Explore-seeded iteration:
 crossover now FIRES, but exploration never reaches the win

Added Go-Explore return-then-explore seeding (genomes share states by construction) +
crossover fire-rate instrumentation + win provenance. Result on the hard tail
(wa30/sb26/su15, budget 5000):

- DIAGNOSIS CONFIRMED + FIXED at the mechanism level: crossover fire-rate 0.15-0.62
  (was ~0 with random seeding); archive 3-5x bigger (46/31/25 vs 9/15/20). The non-AR
  recombination engine now engages.
- BUT still QD-generates-where-BFS-fails = 0/3. The deeper bottleneck is now exposed:
  even with crossover firing, NO winning fragment exists to recombine because
  exploration (even Go-Explore) never reaches the win region. The binding constraint
  is GOAL-DIRECTED exploration-to-first-win, not the recombination mechanism.

Both #1 (perception-gated heuristic) and #2 (coverage-fitness + working crossover)
converge on the same missing piece: a GOAL SIGNAL to steer exploration toward the
(unknown) win -> the goal-induction / active-inference layer is the next lever.

verdict: complete: energy_as_fitness_qd_no_winner_honest_null_gap_sharpened

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
